Wikipedia, it is more important to avoid language that makes undue 
implications.Words to Watch: reveal, point out, clarify, expose, explain, find,
note, observe, insist, speculate, surmise, claim, assert, admit, confess, deny,
confirm ...
17. Euphemisms: Euphemisms should generally be avoided in favor of more neutral
and precise terms.​Words to Watch: passed away, gave her life, eternal rest, 
make love, an issue with, collateral damage, differently abled.
18. Clichés and idioms: Clichés and idioms should generally be avoided in favor
of direct, literal expressions.Words to watch: lion's share, tip of the 
