"20260728144303102308_1e55e79e", "type": "Document", "text": "The article 
reports on gold rings and other objects found in a Mycenaean warrior's grave 
near the Palace of Nestor in Pylos. It says the burial, uncovered in May 2015, 
contained about 2,000 objects and belonged to a man in his mid-30s who died 
around 1500 B.C. The article focuses on four solid gold signet rings and other 
grave goods as evidence that Mycenaean elites were influenced by, exchanged 
with, and adopted aspects of Minoan culture from Crete rather than only 
pillaging it.", "source_id": "20260728144301975480_4af19a92"}, {"id": 
