"Source", "source_type": "official", "title": "Griffin Warrior Tomb - Griffin 
Warrior", "url": "https://griffinwarrior.org/griffin-warrior-tomb"}, {"id": 
"20260728144302055167_8bb5b995", "type": "Document", "text": "This Academia 
page hosts Jack L. Davis's 2016 Hesperia paper titled \"The Lord of the Gold 
Rings: The Griffin Warrior of Pylos.\" The visible abstract says that in May 
2015 a University of Cincinnati team discovered a large stone-built tomb of 
Late Helladic IIA date near Tholos Tomb IV at the Palace of Nestor, Pylos. The 
tomb contained the body of a single male, aged 30-35, with hundreds of grave 
goods including gold, silver, bronze, ivory, and semiprecious stones. Among the
gold objects were four signet rings decorated with Minoan ritual scenes, and 
the paper says it discusses the excavation, describes the rings, and considers 
the significance of their iconography for the Mycenaeans who buried them.", 
"source_id": "20260728144301401021_64c4c49f"}, {"id": 
