article into a general account of the Griffin Warrior burial.', 'content': 'The
ring was reported from a stone-built tomb discovered in May 2015 during renewed
University of Cincinnati excavations near Tholos Tomb IV at the Palace of 
Nestor, Pylos.[1][2] The burial contained the remains of a single male, 
estimated to have been in his 30s, together with a rich assemblage of grave 
goods.[1][2][5] Sources describing the tomb note four gold signet rings among 
the finds, but they discuss the Ring of Nestor only in relation to that broader
context.[1][2][3][4]'}, {'title': 'Description and interpretation', 'key': 
