report says the rings were probably made in Crete and may have been used to 
seal documents or objects, while another notes that the papers on the find 
examine the significance of the rings' iconography for the Mycenaeans who 
buried them.[2][4] The sources also state that the rings are made of multiple 
sheets of gold and depict detailed scenes, but the exact object-level 
